pageType: table
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$paper"
notes: >-
  Walk the four steps in order, about seven minutes each. Frame: one sentence
  that states the problem, the user, and the outcome — write it on the plan.
  Scope: agree what is in and what is out; name one success metric. Owners:
  every decision and deliverable gets exactly one owner; owners can ask for
  help, but they decide. Launch: the first milestone and the first check-in go
  on the calendar before anyone leaves. The AI assistant drafts each step from
  the conversation as it happens, so the plan writes itself and nothing depends
  on anyone's memory. The check: the whole workflow fits on one page and any
  member can read it back.
elements:
  - elementId: t
    elementType: text
    bounds: [46, 36, 840, 46]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      wrap: false
      text: "Four steps to a one-page plan"
  - elementId: tb
    elementType: table
    bounds: [46, 168, 868, 312]
    columnWidths: [0.18, 0.45, 0.37]
    rows:
      - - text: "Step"
        - text: "Answer this"
        - text: "Output"
      - - text: "01 Frame"
        - text: "What problem, for whom, what outcome?"
        - text: "One sentence the team can repeat"
      - - text: "02 Scope"
        - text: "What we build — and what we don't"
        - text: "Scope list + one success metric"
      - - text: "03 Owners"
        - text: "Who decides what, who delivers?"
        - text: "One owner per decision and deliverable"
      - - text: "04 Launch"
        - text: "What starts when, how we check"
        - text: "First milestone + first check-in"
      - - text: "AI assist"
        - text: "Drafts each step from raw notes"
        - text: "The one-page plan, captured live"
